rategically, keeping the essential comparisons in the main text while moving the supplementary analyses to the appendix.\n\nThe requirements specify I need sections and tables for all seven experiments from the data file, so I can't skip anything—but I can be smart about presentation. I'll combine the model comparison tables into a single comprehensive view, keep the condition-specific analyses as the core results, use the interaction and error analysis tables as supporting evidence, and preserve the reliability and validation tables to strengthen the empirical foundation.\n\nI'm going to structure this using the standard ACL format and start drafting the full paper now. I'm mapping out the table structure to cover all seven experiments systematically—clause statistics, violation rates across models, binary effects, type uniformity, visibility patterns, failure modes, reliability metrics, realism validation, and classifier performance. Some tables will be condensed, but this ensures comprehensive coverage.\n\nI realize the model×type interaction from C4 needs its own table too, so I'll need to integrate that into the layout. Now I'm drafting the full LaTeX paper, aiming to keep the main text to eight pages while being thorough.\n\nWriting the paper...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5812,"cache_read_input_tokens":34703,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5812},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"38bd7393-efbc-4b1e-8862-14094f2059ed","uuid":"6353045b-36ca-4024-b0cb-09efc9aaa985"}
